   * explicit `false` turns it off) so existing callers keep applying the wallet first.
   * When the balance doesn't fully cover the term charge — the toggle is off, or the
   * balance is short — the remainder is charged to a card that funds the wallet, then
   * the wallet path (`orderEmailHostingCore`) places the subscription.
   */
  useWallet: boolean = true,
): Promise<Result | { checkout: EmbeddedCheckout }> {
  const user = await requireUser();
  // Spend path: block while an admin is impersonating, so support cannot buy a
  // subscription with a customer's wallet while acting as them. Caught so an
  // impersonating admin sees this message inline instead of a page crash — the
  // bare throw used to hit the wizard's generic error screen on every attempt.
  try {
    await assertNotImpersonating();
  } catch (e) {
    return { error: e instanceof Error ? e.message : "This action is disabled while impersonating a customer." };
  }
  // Purchase gate: an unverified address means we cannot reach the person we
  // are about to charge. See lib/email-verification.ts.
  const unverified = await emailVerificationError(user);
  if (unverified) return { error: unverified };

  const name = String(domainName ?? "")
    .trim()
    .toLowerCase()
    .replace(/\.$/, "");
  if (!name) return { error: "Enter a domain." };
  if (!domainRe.test(name)) return { error: "Enter a valid domain (e.g. example.com)." };

  // Price the term for the wallet/card split. Business Email has no first-month-free,
  // so the amount due today IS the full term charge. Shared `emailChargeCents` with the
  // core below so the split and the debit can never use different formulas.
  const planForSplit = await db.emailPlan.findUnique({ where: { id: emailPlanId } });
  if (!planForSplit || !planForSplit.active) return { error: "That email plan isn't available." };
  const term = normalizeProductTerm(termMonthsRaw);
  const { fullCharge } = await emailChargeCents(planForSplit, term);
  const { cardCents } = walletSplit({ dueCents: fullCharge, balanceCents: user.balanceCents, useWallet });

  if (cardCents > 0) {
    // A card leg is due (the toggle is off, or the balance is short). Reject an already-
    // taken domain BEFORE opening a paid checkout (the core re-checks authoritatively at
    // fulfilment), then fund the remainder by card. On payment `fulfilCheckoutSession`
    // credits the card amount to the wallet and calls `orderEmailHostingCore`, which
    // debits the real charge — one debit path.
    const dupe = await db.emailSubscription.findFirst({ where: { domainName: name, status: { not: "CANCELLED" } } });
    if (dupe) {
